WEBVTT

account-onboarding
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:15.000
Create an account
Choose Google or email. For email, verify the inbox link to continue. Set your optional preferences or skip them.

new-project
00:00:15.000 --> 00:00:30.000
Start a project
In your workspace, choose Websites → New project or Applications → New application. In the public Builder, choose New project. Enter your own idea.

ai-builder
00:00:30.000 --> 00:00:45.000
Build with AI
Describe the result, then choose Build page for a website or Build for an app. Wait for a complete preview and check its source label.

ai-chat
00:00:45.000 --> 00:01:00.000
Refine in chat
Describe one change. In Websites, choose Update page; in Applications, choose Update. Let the update finish before the next change.

design
00:01:00.000 --> 00:01:15.000
Adjust the design
Open Design. A website control starts a refinement. In applications, choose your theme, accent, type and spacing, then Apply design.

preview
00:01:15.000 --> 00:01:30.000
Preview each screen
Use Desktop, Tablet or Mobile to inspect the project. Try app forms with synthetic records, and choose Save to keep a record.

versions
00:01:30.000 --> 00:01:45.000
Restore a version
Once you have revisions, open History, inspect one, then Restore. In apps, this restores the design and structure; data records stay intact.

save-reopen
00:01:45.000 --> 00:02:00.000
Save and reopen
Save on this device keeps a local website. In your signed-in workspace, use Save to account and Saved websites. Data apps save to your account.

connections
00:02:00.000 --> 00:02:15.000
Check connections
In your signed-in workspace, open Integrations for availability and permissions. These tools are not connected here; Google sign-in is separate.

export-publish
00:02:15.000 --> 00:02:30.000
Export or share
Export downloads website HTML or an app ZIP/data. In your workspace, Publishing can share a saved website where enabled; it is not full app hosting.

usage
00:02:30.000 --> 00:02:45.000
Check usage
In your signed-in workspace, open More → Usage for measured build activity. Payments and credit purchases are off; no active checkout is offered.
